WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:01.694
Shopping and Returns.

2
00:00:01.974 --> 00:00:06.369
Day 36 of the Soft Skill Playbook course, in the Everyday Life phase.

3
00:00:08.119 --> 00:00:09.143
The key idea.

4
00:00:09.423 --> 00:00:19.343
Today's goal: shop for clothes and electronics: sizes, colours, trial rooms, warranties, bargaining, and returning or exchanging something that's wrong.

5
00:00:20.693 --> 00:00:21.546
Part 1.

6
00:00:21.826 --> 00:00:22.786
Key words.

7
00:00:24.036 --> 00:00:25.380
Here is a quick table:

8
00:00:25.660 --> 00:00:48.295
Word or phrase, and Meaning. size (S or M or L or XL) / fit (tight, loose): for clothes. trial room or fitting room: where you try clothes on. exchange or return or refund: swap it or give it back or money back. receipt or bill or invoice: proof of purchase. warranty or guarantee: free repair or replacement for a period.

9
00:00:48.575 --> 00:01:00.159
EMI or no-cost EMI: pay in monthly parts. cash on delivery (COD): pay when it arrives. out of stock or pre-order: not available or order before release.

10
00:01:01.509 --> 00:01:02.383
Part 2.

11
00:01:02.663 --> 00:01:03.879
Questions you'll ask.

12
00:01:05.129 --> 00:01:05.961
Clothes.

13
00:01:06.241 --> 00:01:08.460
Do you have this in a medium or in blue?

14
00:01:08.740 --> 00:01:09.956
Can I try this on?

15
00:01:10.236 --> 00:01:11.580
Where's the trial room?

16
00:01:11.860 --> 00:01:13.332
Does it come in other colours?

17
00:01:13.612 --> 00:01:14.700
It's a bit tight.

18
00:01:14.980 --> 00:01:16.388
Do you have a bigger size?

19
00:01:16.668 --> 00:01:17.713
Is this cotton?

20
00:01:17.993 --> 00:01:19.487
Can I wash it in a machine?

21
00:01:20.837 --> 00:01:21.861
Electronics.

22
00:01:22.141 --> 00:01:24.189
What's the difference between these two models?

23
00:01:24.469 --> 00:01:25.962
How long is the warranty?

24
00:01:26.242 --> 00:01:27.927
Is it from the brand or the shop?

25
00:01:28.207 --> 00:01:29.807
Is there an EMI option?

26
00:01:30.087 --> 00:01:31.559
Is it no-cost EMI?

27
00:01:31.839 --> 00:01:33.247
Can you install it at home?

28
00:01:33.527 --> 00:01:34.978
Is installation free?

29
00:01:35.258 --> 00:01:37.050
What's the best price you can give me?

30
00:01:38.400 --> 00:01:39.275
Returns.

31
00:01:39.555 --> 00:01:41.091
What's your return policy?

32
00:01:41.371 --> 00:01:43.440
Can I exchange it for a different size?

33
00:01:43.720 --> 00:01:46.173
Can I get a refund instead of store credit?

34
00:01:46.453 --> 00:01:48.096
How long does the refund take?

35
00:01:49.446 --> 00:01:50.342
Part 3.

36
00:01:50.622 --> 00:01:52.755
Conversation 1: buying a shirt.

37
00:01:54.005 --> 00:01:56.032
Here is how the conversation goes.

38
00:01:56.312 --> 00:01:57.315
Hello!

39
00:01:57.595 --> 00:01:59.259
Can I help you find something?

40
00:01:59.539 --> 00:02:02.611
Yes, I'm looking for a formal shirt for an interview.

41
00:02:02.891 --> 00:02:04.661
These are our new cotton shirts.

42
00:02:04.941 --> 00:02:06.243
What size are you?

43
00:02:06.523 --> 00:02:08.912
Usually a 40, or a large.

44
00:02:09.192 --> 00:02:10.920
Here's a white one in 40.

45
00:02:11.200 --> 00:02:12.757
Would you like to try it on?

46
00:02:14.107 --> 00:02:15.707
The conversation continues.

47
00:02:15.987 --> 00:02:17.054
Yes, please.

48
00:02:17.334 --> 00:02:18.891
Where's the trial room?

49
00:02:19.171 --> 00:02:20.665
Just there, on the right.

50
00:02:20.945 --> 00:02:22.203
A few minutes later

51
00:02:22.483 --> 00:02:24.574
It's a little tight on the shoulders.

52
00:02:24.854 --> 00:02:26.475
Do you have a 42?

53
00:02:26.755 --> 00:02:28.035
Yes, here you go.

54
00:02:28.315 --> 00:02:30.150
It also comes in light blue.

55
00:02:31.500 --> 00:02:33.100
The conversation continues.

56
00:02:33.380 --> 00:02:35.087
The 42 fits well.

57
00:02:35.367 --> 00:02:38.225
I'll take the white one and the light blue one.

58
00:02:38.505 --> 00:02:39.444
Great.

59
00:02:39.724 --> 00:02:40.855
Anything else?

60
00:02:41.135 --> 00:02:42.329
No, that's all.

61
00:02:42.609 --> 00:02:45.447
What's your exchange policy, just in case?

62
00:02:45.727 --> 00:02:48.777
You can exchange within 15 days with the bill and tags.

63
00:02:50.127 --> 00:02:51.045
Part 4.

64
00:02:51.325 --> 00:02:53.799
Conversation 2: returning headphones.

65
00:02:55.049 --> 00:02:57.076
Here is how the conversation goes.

66
00:02:57.356 --> 00:02:58.081
Hi.

67
00:02:58.361 --> 00:03:03.055
I bought these headphones here last week, and the left side has stopped working.

68
00:03:03.335 --> 00:03:04.807
I'm sorry to hear that.

69
00:03:05.087 --> 00:03:06.281
Do you have the bill?

70
00:03:06.561 --> 00:03:07.777
Yes, here it is.

71
00:03:08.057 --> 00:03:09.871
It was the 4th of this month.

72
00:03:10.151 --> 00:03:11.260
Thank you.

73
00:03:11.540 --> 00:03:12.756
Let me test them...

74
00:03:13.036 --> 00:03:14.956
Yes, the left side isn't working.

75
00:03:16.306 --> 00:03:17.906
The conversation continues.

76
00:03:18.186 --> 00:03:20.063
I'd like a replacement, please.

77
00:03:20.343 --> 00:03:23.373
Or a refund, if you don't have the same model.

78
00:03:23.653 --> 00:03:25.637
We have the same model in stock.

79
00:03:25.917 --> 00:03:27.431
I'll replace them for you.

80
00:03:27.711 --> 00:03:28.650
Thank you.

81
00:03:28.930 --> 00:03:31.191
Will the warranty start again from today?

82
00:03:31.471 --> 00:03:35.525
No, it continues from the original date, but the new pair is fully covered.

83
00:03:36.875 --> 00:03:38.475
The conversation continues.

84
00:03:38.755 --> 00:03:39.693
Okay.

85
00:03:39.973 --> 00:03:41.744
Could you write that on the bill?

86
00:03:42.024 --> 00:03:42.728
Sure.

87
00:03:44.078 --> 00:03:45.038
Part 5.

88
00:03:45.318 --> 00:03:46.491
When things go wrong.

89
00:03:47.741 --> 00:03:49.917
The size is wrong in my online order.

90
00:03:50.197 --> 00:03:51.392
How do I return it?

91
00:03:51.672 --> 00:03:53.549
The colour is different from the photo.

92
00:03:53.829 --> 00:03:55.557
It was damaged when it arrived.

93
00:03:55.837 --> 00:03:57.096
Here are the photos.

94
00:03:57.376 --> 00:03:59.808
You said I could return it within 15 days.

95
00:04:00.088 --> 00:04:02.200
Could I speak to the store manager, please?

96
00:04:03.550 --> 00:04:04.489
Part 6.

97
00:04:04.769 --> 00:04:05.686
Practice.

98
00:04:06.936 --> 00:04:08.109
Rewrite politely:

99
00:04:08.389 --> 00:04:12.443
Show me other colour. / I want my money back. / Give discount.

100
00:04:13.793 --> 00:04:14.710
Success:

101
00:04:14.990 --> 00:04:15.843
Answers.

102
00:04:16.123 --> 00:04:21.926
Could you show me other colours? / I'd like a refund, please. / Is there any discount on this?

103
00:04:23.276 --> 00:04:24.215
Part 7.

104
00:04:24.495 --> 00:04:25.540
Speak today.

105
00:04:26.790 --> 00:04:29.627
Ask about size, colour or warranty at a shop.

106
00:04:29.907 --> 00:04:33.129
Ask What's your return policy? before your next purchase.

107
00:04:34.479 --> 00:04:36.015
That's the end of this lesson.

108
00:04:36.295 --> 00:04:40.945
Pick one script from it, say it out loud three times, and use it for real today.

109
00:04:41.225 --> 00:04:47.348
For extra practice, paste the Master Prompt into an AI assistant and role-play the conversation.

